{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1793897640912, "sessionID": "ses_e535e9ef0ffeVDCZbY8Rg9lJyb", "part": {"id": "prt_1aca1a166001M4ZioJ56YBuKpI", "messageID": "msg_1aca199080016amamg5g5qQ2DU", "sessionID": "ses_e535e9ef0ffeVDCZbY8Rg9lJyb", "type": "text", "text": "**OrderService** and **RenewalsWorker** call **PaymentsAPI** directly.\n\n**The available architecture data does not establish why PaymentsService never retries a declined payment.** Its configuration lists only `PAYMENT_API_KEY` and `CAPTURE_TIMEOUT`; neither returned statement describes retry behavior or handling of declines. Explaining that behavior would require PaymentsService\u2019s payment-handling code or a documented retry policy.\n\nFor completeness, the dependency lookup also identifies:\n- **NotificationsAPI**, exposed by **NotificationsService**, which PaymentsService calls.\n- **PaymentsPostgresDatabase**, where PaymentsService stores data.\n- **NotificationsRedisInstance**, where NotificationsService stores data.\n\nNone of those returned relationships explains the no-retry behavior.", "time": {"start": 1793897636198, "end": 1793897640910}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "msg_0135b962785afccf016aecb4a4222487d1bfca676b21fbf12c", "phase": "final_answer"}}}}
